    <briefdescription>
<para>A function to parse an integer or an array of integers, a real or an array of reals, a string or an array of strings. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Parse is an integer function that decodes values from a text string. The text string has the form: &quot;label=list&quot; where &quot;label&quot; is an arbitrary user defined label describing the values being decoded, and &quot;list&quot; is a list of one or more values separated by commas. The values may be integer, real, or character. Parse returns the number of values decoded. <linebreak/>
Example usage: <programlisting filename=".F90"><codeline><highlight class="normal">number<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="interfacefield__manager__mod_1_1parse" kindref="compound">parse</ref>(text,<sp/>label,<sp/></highlight><highlight class="keywordtype">value</highlight><highlight class="normal">)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>    </detaileddescription>
